### Part IX — Extensions for IDEs

An editor runs its extensions in its own host, not a process Loom starts. This part is what each editor needs to read a loom. VS Code gets an extension, a client that bridges the editor to Loom's language server. Every other editor gets a tree-sitter grammar for colour and a few lines of configuration that start the same server with `loom lsp`, written first for Neovim and Helix.

